<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alp Arslan al-Akhras</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1114</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alp-arslan">Alp Arslan</a> al-Akhras, 'the Mute', was the Seljuk ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a> for about a year after his father Ridwan's death in 1113. A puppet of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eunuch">eunuch</a> Lu'lu', he had many of his father's officials and the city's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/order-of-assassins">Assassins</a> killed, and was murdered by Lu'lu' in 1114.</p></div>
